From a379d089837d691f8241c3a0f23641da5023b856 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Neil Johnson <neil.johnson71@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 11:57:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 13/26] aslink: a module with no .cdb file is not an error

SDCDBcopy() copies each module's cdb file into the linker's own cdb
output.  It already treats a missing one as nothing to copy - the whole
body is guarded by "if (xfp)" - but it asked afile() for the file in the
mode that reports a failure to open as an error and counts it in lkerr.
So the normal case was diagnosed as a fault, and, because lkerr decides
the exit status, it failed the link.

Every module a compiler ships in its libraries is built without
debugging information and has no cdb file, so this fired for any -y link
against a library:  sdcc -mz80 --debug produced correct output - map,
NoICE, cdb and hex all written - and still exited 1, with one
"?ASlink-Error-<cannot open>" per library module pulled in.  sdld, whose
lklibr/lksdcdb descend from this same source, has always been silent
here and exits 0.

afile() had no way to be quiet:  bit 4 of its wf argument downgrades the
report from an error to a warning, but a warning is still wrong for a
file whose absence is normal, and it would be one per module.  Bit 16
now suppresses the report entirely, and SDCDBcopy() is its only user.
The bits are documented in afile()'s header comment, which had never
listed them.

The two masking effects that hid this are worth recording.  A module
whose name matches the linker's own cdb output - module one, before -o+
existed to name that output separately - opened the file the linker was
writing rather than a missing one, so it neither failed nor copied
anything sensible.  And a link of a single module is the case most often
tested by hand.

Verified:
  - New case optcdb:  -y over a module ascheck built, which therefore
    has no cdb file, must link clean and still write the linker's cdb.
    It fails against master's aslink and passes against this one, with
    the other 19 cases passing in both.
  - make check 20/20;  the 19 pre-existing goldens are unchanged.
  - sdcc -mz80 --debug against the z80 library goes from exit 1 with 3
    diagnostics to exit 0 with none, still writing .cdb, .map, .noi and
    .ihx.  Without --debug the link is unchanged.
  - Clean under -fsanitize=address,undefined for -y alone, -y with -o+,
    and -y over two modules;  no new -Wall -Wextra warning.
---
 linksrc/lkmain.c  | 8 ++++++++
 linksrc/lksdcdb.c | 7 ++++++-
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/linksrc/lkmain.c b/linksrc/lkmain.c
index bd53654..5e0f4f2 100644
--- a/linksrc/lkmain.c
+++ b/linksrc/lkmain.c
@@ -1462,6 +1462,11 @@ setgbl(void)
  *
  *	side effects:
  *		File is opened for read or write.
+ *
+ *	The wf argument is a bit field:  1 selects write, 2 binary,
+ *	4 downgrades a failure to open from an error to a warning,
+ *	8 keeps an extension already present in fn, and 16 reports
+ *	nothing at all - for a file whose absence is not a fault.
  */
 
 FILE *
@@ -1531,6 +1536,9 @@ afile(char *fn, char *ft, int wf)
 	case 3:	frmt = "wb";	break;
 	}
 	if ((fp = fopen(afspec, frmt)) == NULL) {
+		if (wf & 16) {
+			;
+		} else
 		if (wf & 4) {
 			fprintf(stderr, "?ASlink-Warning-<cannot %s> : \"%s\"\n", (frmt[0] == 'w')?"create":"open", afspec);
 		} else {
diff --git a/linksrc/lksdcdb.c b/linksrc/lksdcdb.c
index 7b1fbe3..f1279f2 100644
--- a/linksrc/lksdcdb.c
+++ b/linksrc/lksdcdb.c
@@ -111,7 +111,12 @@ void SDCDBcopy(char *str)
 	 * Copy cdb file if present and requested.
 	 */
 	if (yflag && yfp) {
-		xfp = afile(str,"cdb",0);
+		/*
+		 * A module compiled without debugging information has no
+		 * cdb file.  That is not a fault - the loop below simply
+		 * has nothing to copy - so the open is made silently.
+		 */
+		xfp = afile(str,"cdb",16);
 		if (xfp) {
 			while (fgets(line, sizeof(line), xfp) != NULL) {
 				fprintf(yfp, "%s", line);
